{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>About six hundred thousand men on foot, etc.</b> This expression indicates that they were not a complete six hundred thousand. And since the Torah did not specify the precise count — how many the men actually were, or how many they fell short of the six hundred thousand — it appears proper to say that they were short by only one, and He did not wish to state their number with the deficiency." "<b>And thus</b> I found in Pirkei R. Eliezer, chapter 39: When Israel went up from Egypt, all the men were reckoned — sixty myriad less one. What did the Holy One, blessed be He, do? He entered into the count with them, and their number came to sixty myriad, as it is said (Genesis 46:4): ״ואנכי אעלך גם עלה״ — 'and I will surely bring you up'; 'also I shall go up' — end of quote."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:18.809743575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}